{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793807157,"nonce":"wngm7h147E3PJZqpnGn6Yo8VkGI=","title":"Tiering: let static-hot first calls interpret while Cranelift compiles","message":"The static-hot branch in BindingParts::tick_callback calls try_lazy_compile synchronously on first entry, waiting for whole-function HIR optimization and Cranelift code. This bypasses the existing lowered interpreter body and makes lua$chunk preparation a startup barrier. The intended TieredRuntime policy is to execute lowered IR (with required release insertion) while background compilation proceeds, then transfer the running loop through OSR.\n\nRemove the blocking static-hot entry override; preserve background preparation, normal call hotness and live-loop OSR. Replace the old static_hot_precompile regression that demanded native code on first entry with a test proving no optimization is necessary to start interpreting. Verify actual transfer from the lowered Lua chunk, correctness across tiers, the full pinned official TS corpus, and NUC short/long benchmarks with frozen binaries and no builds between samples.\n\nRelated premature LLVM-profitability work remains separate: e4a4a9cba130ac5253b63a593c6ed9e570db9ca5a24ac692f292a73bbe141f74. Do not close that broader issue just for changing first-call dispatch.","files":null}]}